WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.279
Besides its fields, a ticket can have sections: bigger parts, like a timer, file uploads, or links to other tickets. In this video, you’ll choose which ticket types get which sections.

2
00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:24.100
In Work Configuration, open Ticket Types. The Sections column shows the sections each type has. A checklist has none, while a maintenance request has time logging and file uploads.

3
00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:30.187
Click a type’s sections to change them. Each section has a switch, and your change saves straight away.

4
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:41.215
Built in are Time logging, with a clock and time entries; Attach files; Hierarchy, for parent and child tickets; and Linked tickets. Let’s turn on linked tickets for repairs.

5
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:46.467
Apps like GitHub, Claude and Cursor appear here too, once they’re connected in Apps.

6
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:54.976
Every section starts off, so simple tickets stay simple. Turning one off hides it on every ticket of that type, but nothing is deleted.

7
00:00:55.767 --> 00:01:02.039
On the ticket, its sections show below the fields. Here’s the time logged on this repair, and its attachments.

8
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:15.267
That’s sections. Next in the Admin console series: choosing which ticket types each location, project or product can use. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

